/T (Looking forward, Emily crystallized the challenges and opportunities ahead. The biggest hurdle remains fragmentation and the stop-start costs of running infrastructure end-to-end, as each market requires separate regulatory compliance, banking relationships, and technical integrations. Yet this challenge presents the biggest opportunity: connecting financial rails, banks, and e-commerce platforms to unlock real-world use cases. By unifying liquidity across these fragmented systems and bridging traditional infrastructure with blockchain efficiency, stablecoins can finally drive mainstream adoption beyond speculation into everyday financial activity.)
